  <h1>The Man Who Saved a Billion Lives</h1>
  <p class="dek">In 1968, a Stanford professor wrote a book predicting hundreds of millions would starve to death. The world believed him. But the man who proved him wrong was an Iowa farm boy breeding wheat in a Mexican field.</p>
